# NOTICE (English)

## What the license covers

Code and original written content in this repository are released under the MIT License — full text in [`LICENSE`](LICENSE). That includes all of the summary text we wrote in the places listed below.

## Content summarizing third-party sources

These parts of the repo introduce or verify things others have published:

- `translations/`: the directory name is a holdover from early planning; its contents are not translations but summaries and verification **written in our own words** after reading a third party's public benchmark, article, post or repo.
- [`capability-map.en.md`](capability-map.en.md), [`browser-automation.en.md`](browser-automation.en.md), [`jev-variants.en.md`](jev-variants.en.md), and the comparison sections of the README: organizing third-party projects' approaches and numbers, with links to the originals.

All of this content:

- Reproduces no full text and translates nothing paragraph by paragraph; direct quotation is limited to short, attributed phrases.
- Links to the originals so readers can check them; each `translations/` entry also states its reproduction scope in `SOURCE.md`.
- Leaves rights in the quoted material with its authors; the MIT License does not extend to it.

If an original author considers anything here beyond fair quotation, please open an issue and we'll revise or remove it.

## Contributing new content

Write it up in your own words; don't paste in the original's full text or translate it paragraph by paragraph. If you must reproduce more than short phrases (e.g. full test items), first confirm the original license permits redistribution and record it in `SOURCE.md`. The full inclusion rules are in [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md).

## Data used by the suites

Each suite's README states the source, license and handling of the data it uses:

- Public datasets are used under their original licenses (e.g. PhysioNet/CinC Challenge 2015 under ODC-By; typed-decisions under Apache 2.0; MASSIVE under CC BY 4.0). Dataset text isn't committed unless necessary; receipts store only case IDs and model outputs.
- Data taken from private systems is de-identified first, with the handling described in that suite's README.

